IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpcnt-dates`
IMPORT `lpcnt-costs`

-- Legal Profession Act 2006 (NT), costs agreements -- worked cases for every exported question.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text (reprint REPL007), section by section, never copied from
-- the encoding's output. The client in most cases is Mia, injured at work in Darwin, who is offered a "no win, no fee"
-- conditional costs agreement with a 25% uplift fee for her compensation claim. The uplift cap of s 319(4) is set by
-- the Legal Profession Regulations (NT), which are not deposited; the cases take 25% as the input.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases`

-- The provisions as the answers name them (the wording of each entry; which entries appear is what is worked by hand).
`P 317(2)` MEANS "s 317(2): the costs agreement is not written or evidenced in writing"
`P 317(4)` MEANS "s 317(4): the written offer does not clearly specify that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement, that it can be accepted in writing or by other conduct, and the type of conduct that will constitute acceptance"
`P 317(5)` MEANS "s 317(5): the costs agreement provides that the legal costs are not subject to costs assessment, and you are not a sophisticated client who may contract out under s 343"
`P 318(2)(a)` MEANS "s 318(2)(a): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves criminal proceedings"
`P 318(2)(b)` MEANS "s 318(2)(b): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)"
`P 318(2)(c)` MEANS "s 318(2)(c): a conditional costs agreement may not relate to a matter that involves proceedings prescribed by the regulations"
`P 318(3)(a)` MEANS "s 318(3)(a): it does not set out the circumstances that constitute the successful outcome of the matter"
`P 318(3)(c)(i)` MEANS "s 318(3)(c)(i): it is not in writing"
`P 318(3)(c)(ii)` MEANS "s 318(3)(c)(ii): it is not in clear plain language"
`P 318(3)(c)(iii)` MEANS "s 318(3)(c)(iii): it is not signed by you"
`P 318(3)(d)` MEANS "s 318(3)(d): it does not state that you were informed of your right to seek independent legal advice before entering into it"
`P 318(3)(e)` MEANS "s 318(3)(e): it does not contain a cooling-off period of at least 5 clear business days"
`P 319(1)` MEANS "s 319(1): the uplift fee includes an amount for disbursements"
`P 319(2)` MEANS "s 319(2): the basis of calculation of the uplift fee is not separately identified"
`P 319(3)` MEANS "s 319(3): no estimate of the uplift fee is specified (nor, where an estimate is not reasonably practicable, a range of estimates and an explanation of the major variables)"
`P 319(4)` MEANS "s 319(4): in a litigious matter the uplift fee exceeds the percentage prescribed by the regulations of the legal costs (excluding disbursements) otherwise payable"
`P 320(1)` MEANS "s 320(1): the amount payable is calculated by reference to the amount of an award or settlement or the value of property recovered (a contingency fee)"

`PI` MEANS `any other matter, such as a personal injury or compensation claim`

-- Asks the two exported s 322(1) questions with every field of a set of facts.
GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ask which` a MEANS
    `s 322(1) -- which provisions does my costs agreement contravene` (a's `how made`) (a's `offer says it is an offer`) (a's `offer says it can be accepted in writing or by conduct`) (a's `offer says what conduct is acceptance`) (a's `says costs are not subject to assessment`) (a's `client listed in s 306(1)(c)`) (a's `costs agreed by tender`) (a's `payment conditional on success`) (a's `kind of matter`) (a's `sets out what counts as success`) (a's `in clear plain language`) (a's `signed by the client`) (a's `has independent advice statement`) (a's `cooling-off business days`) (a's `has uplift fee`) (a's `uplift fee includes disbursements`) (a's `uplift basis separately identified`) (a's `uplift estimate specified`) (a's `uplift estimate not reasonably practicable`) (a's `uplift range of estimates specified`) (a's `uplift major variables explained`) (a's `litigious`) (a's `uplift percentage`) (a's `prescribed uplift percentage`) (a's `calculated by reference to recovery`) (a's `adopts a fixed costs provision`)

GIVEN a IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ask void` a MEANS
    `s 322(1) -- is my costs agreement void` (a's `how made`) (a's `offer says it is an offer`) (a's `offer says it can be accepted in writing or by conduct`) (a's `offer says what conduct is acceptance`) (a's `says costs are not subject to assessment`) (a's `client listed in s 306(1)(c)`) (a's `costs agreed by tender`) (a's `payment conditional on success`) (a's `kind of matter`) (a's `sets out what counts as success`) (a's `in clear plain language`) (a's `signed by the client`) (a's `has independent advice statement`) (a's `cooling-off business days`) (a's `has uplift fee`) (a's `uplift fee includes disbursements`) (a's `uplift basis separately identified`) (a's `uplift estimate specified`) (a's `uplift estimate not reasonably practicable`) (a's `uplift range of estimates specified`) (a's `uplift major variables explained`) (a's `litigious`) (a's `uplift percentage`) (a's `prescribed uplift percentage`) (a's `calculated by reference to recovery`) (a's `adopts a fixed costs provision`)

-- The argument order of `the agreement`: how made; offer says it is an offer; offer says acceptance; offer says conduct;
-- excludes assessment; listed in s 306(1)(c); tender; conditional; matter; success set out; plain; signed; advice
-- statement; cooling-off days; uplift; uplift includes disbursements; uplift basis; uplift estimate; estimate
-- impracticable; range; variables; litigious; uplift %; prescribed %; by reference to recovery; fixed costs provision.

-- Mia's agreement: written, signed, plain, success defined, advice statement, 5 clear business days' cooling off, a
-- 25% uplift with its basis and an estimate, in a litigious compensation claim, cap 25%. Meets every requirement.
`Mia` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE

-- Variants, each changing what its comment says.
-- Oral, nothing in writing: s 317(2), and a conditional agreement not in writing, s 318(3)(c)(i).
`oral` MEANS `the agreement` `an oral agreement with nothing in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- A written offer accepted by conduct, which does not say what conduct is acceptance: s 317(4) only.
`offer without conduct` MEANS `the agreement` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- A complying written offer: nothing.
`offer complete` MEANS `the agreement` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Oral but evidenced in writing: passes s 317(2) but a conditional agreement must be "in writing": s 318(3)(c)(i).
`evidenced` MEANS `the agreement` `an oral agreement evidenced in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Says costs are not subject to assessment: s 317(5).
`no assessment` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- The same, costs agreed by tender (sophisticated client, s 343): nothing.
`no assessment, tender` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Criminal proceedings: s 318(2)(a).
`criminal` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `criminal proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Success not defined, not plain language: s 318(3)(a), (c)(ii).
`vague` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Not signed, no advice statement, 4 days' cooling off: s 318(3)(c)(iii), (d), (e).
`unsigned` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- The same with a client listed in s 306(1)(c) (s 318(5)): nothing.
`unsigned, listed` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 4 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Uplift 25.01% against a 25% cap in a litigious matter: s 319(4).
`over cap` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25.01 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Uplift 40% in a matter not litigious: s 319(4) does not apply: nothing.
`over cap, not litigious` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Uplift on disbursements, basis not identified, no estimate (an estimate was practicable): s 319(1), (2), (3).
`bad uplift` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- No estimate, but not reasonably practicable, with a range and an explanation: nothing.
`range instead` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- A contingency fee (30% of the settlement): s 320(1).
`contingency` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 TRUE FALSE
-- The same, but only adopting an applicable fixed costs provision: nothing.
`fixed scale` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE PI TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 TRUE TRUE
-- An ordinary hourly-rate agreement, not conditional, no uplift, unsigned, no cooling-off: s 318 does not apply: nothing.
`hourly` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE PI FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Not stated as conditional, but with an uplift fee (fork F6): treated as conditional, so s 318(3)(c)(iii), (d), (e).
`uplift only` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE PI TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 FALSE FALSE
-- Family Law Act proceedings and a contingency fee: s 318(2)(b) then s 320(1), in that order.
`family and contingency` MEANS `the agreement` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 25 TRUE FALSE

§§ `s 317(1) -- who may make a costs agreement`

#ASSERT `s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a parent who has contracted with the law practice to pay the child's costs: associated third party payer, s 317(1)(d)
#ASSERT `s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an insurer obliged to the client (not to the law practice): non-associated; s 317(1) does not name it
#ASSERT `s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 317(1) -- may I make a costs agreement with this law practice` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 296 -- who I am` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a non-associated third party payer`

§§ `s 317(2) to (4) -- form`

#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `an oral agreement evidenced in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `an oral agreement with nothing in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written offer accepted in writing or by other conduct` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- the offer questions are not read for a written agreement
#ASSERT `s 317(2) to (4) -- is my costs agreement in a form the Act allows` `a written agreement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 317(5) and s 343 -- costs assessment cannot be excluded`

#ASSERT `s 317(5) and s 343 -- may my costs agreement take my costs outside costs assessment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 317(5) and s 343 -- may my costs agreement take my costs outside costs assessment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 317(5) and s 343 -- may my costs agreement take my costs outside costs assessment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 318(2) -- matters a conditional costs agreement may relate to`

#ASSERT `s 318(2) -- may my costs agreement be conditional on success` PI EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 318(2) -- may my costs agreement be conditional on success` `criminal proceedings` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 318(2) -- may my costs agreement be conditional on success` `proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cth)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 318(2) -- may my costs agreement be conditional on success` `proceedings prescribed by the regulations` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 318(2) to (5) -- what a conditional costs agreement must be and contain`

-- Mia's agreement: nothing missing.
#ASSERT null (`s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` PI `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE)
-- exactly 5 clear business days is enough ("not less than 5")
#ASSERT `s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` PI `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `P 318(3)(e)`
#ASSERT null (`s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` PI `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` PI `an oral agreement evidenced in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `P 318(3)(c)(i)`
#ASSERT `s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` `proceedings prescribed by the regulations` `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `P 318(2)(c)`
-- everything missing, in the order of s 318
#ASSERT `s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` `criminal proceedings` `an oral agreement with nothing in writing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `P 318(2)(a)`, `P 318(3)(a)`, `P 318(3)(c)(i)`, `P 318(3)(c)(ii)`, `P 318(3)(c)(iii)`, `P 318(3)(d)`, `P 318(3)(e)`
-- a sophisticated client (s 318(5)): signature, advice statement and cooling-off not required; the rest still are
#ASSERT `s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` `criminal proceedings` `an oral agreement with nothing in writing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `P 318(2)(a)`, `P 318(3)(a)`, `P 318(3)(c)(i)`, `P 318(3)(c)(ii)`
#ASSERT null (`s 318 -- what my conditional costs agreement fails to meet` PI `a written agreement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of the cooling-off period`

-- Made Friday 6 November 2026, 5 clear business days, no public holiday: Mon 9, Tue 10, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13.
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (`the calendar date` 13 11 2026)
-- the same with a public holiday on Tuesday 10 November: Mon 9, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13, Mon 16.
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 (LIST (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026)) EQUALS JUST (`the calendar date` 16 11 2026)
-- Made Wednesday 23 December 2026, holidays 25 and 28 December and 1 January: Thu 24, Tue 29, Wed 30, Thu 31, Mon 4 Jan.
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 23 12 2026) 5 (LIST (`the calendar date` 25 12 2026), (`the calendar date` 28 12 2026), (`the calendar date` 1 1 2027)) EQUALS JUST (`the calendar date` 4 1 2027)
-- Made on Saturday 7 November 2026: the clear days start on Monday 9: Mon 9 to Fri 13.
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 7 11 2026) 5 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (`the calendar date` 13 11 2026)
-- A 10-day period from Friday 6 November 2026: Mon 9 ... Fri 13, Mon 16 ... Fri 20.
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 10 EMPTY EQUALS JUST (`the calendar date` 20 11 2026)
#ASSERT `s 318(3)(e) -- the last day of my cooling-off period` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 0 EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 318(6)(b) -- ending the agreement in the cooling-off period and the uplift fee`

-- Last day Friday 13 November 2026.
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 12 11 2026) EQUALS `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 13 11 2026) EQUALS `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 14 11 2026) EQUALS `s 318(6) does not apply: your notice came after the cooling-off period ended (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 16 11 2026) EQUALS `s 318(6) does not apply: your notice came after the cooling-off period ended (the text's no)`
-- with the holiday on 10 November the last day is Monday 16 November
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 (LIST (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026)) (`the calendar date` 16 11 2026) EQUALS `No: you ended the agreement within the cooling-off period, so the law practice may not recover the uplift fee (s 318(6)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 (LIST (`the calendar date` 10 11 2026)) (`the calendar date` 17 11 2026) EQUALS `s 318(6) does not apply: your notice came after the cooling-off period ended (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 5 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) EQUALS `s 318(6) does not apply: the notice is dated before the agreement was made`
#ASSERT `s 318(6)(b) -- if I end it on this day, can the law practice still charge the uplift fee` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) 0 EMPTY (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `s 318(6) does not apply: the agreement gives no cooling-off period (it fails s 318(3)(e) unless you are a sophisticated client)`

-- The regulative rule alone: 7 days to the last day. Notice on day 7 then a claim for the uplift fee: breach by the law
-- practice (not FULFILLED). Notice on day 8: the period had passed, the agreement stands (FULFILLED).
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the uplift fee is barred after notice on day` t MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the cooling-off period` 7) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the client` `give written notice terminating the conditional costs agreement` t), (EVENT `the law practice` `recover the uplift fee` t))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

#ASSERT `the uplift fee is barred after notice on day` 0
#ASSERT `the uplift fee is barred after notice on day` 6
#ASSERT `the uplift fee is barred after notice on day` 7
#ASSERT NOT (`the uplift fee is barred after notice on day` 8)

