§§ `s 322(2) to (6) -- what is recovered and repaid under a void agreement`

-- Not void: s 322 does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `it is not void` 20000 5000 18000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it is not void` 20000 5000 18000 25000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 320: nothing recoverable; all $12,000 paid is repaid (s 322(5)).
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320` 20000 0 18000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it charges a contingency fee contrary to s 320` 20000 0 18000 12000 0 EQUALS JUST 12000
-- s 319: agreement $20,000 + $5,000 uplift; fair value $18,000: recover $18,000; paid $25,000 of which $5,000 uplift:
-- repay the $5,000 uplift (s 322(4)) and the $2,000 above $18,000 (s 322(3)): $7,000.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `its uplift fee contravenes s 319` 20000 5000 18000 EQUALS JUST 18000
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `its uplift fee contravenes s 319` 20000 5000 18000 25000 5000 EQUALS JUST 7000
-- s 319, fair value $22,000: capped at the $20,000 the agreement gave without uplift (fork F7); repay the $5,000 uplift.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `its uplift fee contravenes s 319` 20000 5000 22000 EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `its uplift fee contravenes s 319` 20000 5000 22000 25000 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- Another contravention: fair value $15,000 against $20,000 agreed: recover $15,000; paid $20,000: repay $5,000.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `it contravenes another provision of Division 5` 20000 0 15000 EQUALS JUST 15000
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it contravenes another provision of Division 5` 20000 0 15000 20000 0 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- paid only $10,000: nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it contravenes another provision of Division 5` 20000 0 15000 10000 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- paid exactly the $15,000 recoverable: nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `s 322 -- how much must the law practice repay me` `it contravenes another provision of Division 5` 20000 0 15000 15000 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- fair value $30,000 against $20,000 + $5,000 uplift (no s 319 contravention): capped at $25,000 (s 322(3)).
#ASSERT `s 322 -- the most the law practice may recover from me` `it contravenes another provision of Division 5` 20000 5000 30000 EQUALS JUST 25000

§§ `s 339 -- assessment by the agreement's amounts or rates`

#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 339 -- must the costs assessor hold to my agreement's amounts or rates` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 323 -- setting aside`

#ASSERT `s 323 -- can my costs agreement be set aside` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Yes: on your application, the costs assessor may order the costs agreement set aside, and must then fix the fair and reasonable costs (s 323(1), (4), (5))`
#ASSERT `s 323 -- can my costs agreement be set aside` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `No: the costs assessor is not satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable, so s 323(1) gives no order (the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 323 -- can my costs agreement be set aside` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Yes: on your application, the costs assessor may order the costs agreement set aside, and must then fix the fair and reasonable costs (s 323(1), (4), (5))`
#ASSERT `s 323 -- can my costs agreement be set aside` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 323 does not give you an application: you are not a client of the law practice nor an associated third party payer who made the agreement without the client`

-- s 323(6): fair costs $18,000 against $20,000 under the agreement: $18,000; $25,000 against $20,000: $20,000.
#ASSERT `s 323(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after a set-aside` 18000 20000 EQUALS 18000
#ASSERT `s 323(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after a set-aside` 25000 20000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 323(6) -- the most I can be ordered to pay after a set-aside` 20000 20000 EQUALS 20000

§§ `s 352(2)(a) -- 28 days to seek review`

-- Determination Friday 6 November 2026: the 28th day after is Friday 4 December 2026.
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- the last day to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 4 12 2026
-- across the year end: 10 December 2026 + 28 = 7 January 2027
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- the last day to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 10 12 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 7 1 2027
-- a leap year: 1 February 2028 + 28 = 29 February 2028
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- the last day to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 1 2 2028) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `In time: within 28 days after the s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 3 12 2026) EQUALS `In time: within 28 days after the s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 4 12 2026) EQUALS `In time: within 28 days after the s 323 determination (s 352(2)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 5 12 2026) EQUALS `Out of time unless the reviewer allows further time (s 352(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 352(2)(a) -- am I in time to seek review of a set-aside determination` (`the calendar date` 6 11 2026) (`the calendar date` 5 11 2026) EQUALS `The determination has not yet been made on that day`
